            <ArticleTitle>A rare presentation of Spigelian hernia involving the appendix.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>141-143</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ejro.2017.11.002</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spigelian hernia (SH) is a rare entity accounting for 1-2% of ventral abdominal wall hernias. Elusive clinical signs and symptoms pose a diagnostic challenge and a consequent risk of strangulation. We present an emergent case of a Spigelian hernia involving the appendix.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
